Add synchronous require() of ES modules through the shell module registry.

__kandeloNodeNative.__kandeloRequireModule(path) loads, links and evaluates
an ES module through the same registry as import and import(), and returns
its namespace. A pending top-level await throws ERR_REQUIRE_ASYNC_MODULE; a
cyclic require of an evaluating module returns the live partial namespace.

ESR 153 rebase: the shell loader now implements HostLoadImportedModule.
ModuleLink requires LoadRequestedModules to have loaded the static import
graph first, and rejects modules in the new `New` status. A fresh (`New`) or
`Unlinked` module is therefore loaded and linked with LoadRequestedModules
plus the loader's LoadResolved/LoadRejected callbacks, as loadAndExecute
does. loadAndParse also no longer accepts a null module request, so this
builds an evaluation-phase JavaScript request the way loadRootModule does.

